        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(github-copilot): add native web search for Copilot GPT models",
        "body": "Closes #78573\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nGitHub Copilot Responses models can use hosted web search, but OpenClaw only exposed the managed `web_search` path, so users needed another search provider.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nCopilot catalog entries from OpenAI or Azure OpenAI that advertise Responses and tool calls now carry `nativeWebSearchTool`. The Copilot wrapper uses native `web_search` only for that capability and only when no managed provider is pinned. Other models keep the existing route. No OpenAI, core, or public Plugin SDK changes.\n\n## User Impact\n\nSupported Copilot models can search the web through the user's Copilot subscription. Explicit managed providers, tool policy, and unsupported models behave as before.\n\n## Evidence\n\nExact head `ea63ab2afc` was run through the real Copilot provider wrapper and streaming Responses transport without starting the Gateway:\n\n```text\nnative          tool=web_search          effort=low     http=200 terminal=stop citation=www.weather.gov\nbrave pinned    tool=function:web_search effort=minimal\npolicy denied   tool=function:web_search effort=minimal\nno capability   tool=function:web_search effort=minimal\n```\n\nA current Copilot catalog probe completed `web_search_call` for all 9 OpenAI-family Responses models tested: `gpt-5-mini`, `gpt-5.3-codex`, `gpt-5.4`, `gpt-5.4-mini`, `gpt-5.4-nano`, `gpt-5.5`, and the three `gpt-5.6` variants. `gpt-5-mini` and `gpt-5.5` returned `url_citation` output.\n\nValidation passed: 124 changed tests, full type/lint/format/architecture checks, docs checks, `git diff --check`, and full build.\n",
